# The words of the window of FreeSynergy Activities, English (ADR 0057: MessageFormat 2). Every id needs a German twin in de.mf2.
app-name = FreeSynergy Activities
app-tagline = Goal: See what happened in your programs: one timeline of activities, newest first, as a short summary and never the content. The index is yours and stays local.
soon = coming soon
state-connected = The server answers and speaks the contract {$contract}.
state-down = No server is running: {$reason}
state-contract = This frontend does not fit the server: {$reason}
state-hint-down = Start the program with the command fs-activities; it starts the server and this window.
state-hint-contract = Install a matching version of FreeSynergy Activities; the window below only shows what is planned.
today-title = What it can do today
today-1 = Opens this window, finds its server and checks that both speak the same contract version.
today-2 = Says plainly what is not there yet; nothing here pretends to work.
today-3 = The core (timeline, filters, summaries, forgetting) exists as a library and is not wired to this window yet; the server only reports what it offers, which is nothing yet.
coming-title = What comes
coming-1 = Timeline: newest first, grouped by day, with the short text, the program and the time; a click opens the object in its program.
coming-2 = Filters: by program, object type, period and words in the text.
coming-3 = Filter "By me" and "By others": while the hub does not yet deliver who did it, the filter says openly "The source does not yet deliver who it was" and is never greyed out silently.
coming-4 = Summaries: many changes to one object become one line that opens up ("12 changes to page X, 10 to 11 o'clock").
coming-5 = Details per entry: when, from where and by which way it was recorded.
coming-6 = Source missing: a visible message and "Reconnect" instead of an empty list.
coming-7 = Forget: single entries, by filter or by period, with a question first; the log of the hub stays untouched, and the window says so.
coming-8 = A feed of your own timeline as Atom (the standard), only on your request, with a secret address. Comes later.
coming-9 = More, each planned, not scheduled, no promise: an Activities tab inside other programs, a calendar overview of the year, pausing the recording, deleting automatically by age, notifications, export.
menu-program = Activities
menu-new = Timeline
menu-accounts = Forget
menu-search = Search
menu-filter = Filter
menu-all = All
menu-mine = By me
menu-others = By others
who-missing = The source does not yet deliver who it was
menu-chosen = Chosen: {$entry}
screen-start = Start
screen-coming = What comes
status-ready = Ready
